{"tool_name":"needle-api-ebi","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"needle-api-ebi","home":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/services/psa/emboss_needle_rest","summary":"Pairwise sequence alignment of DNA or protein sequences using Needleman-Wunsch global alignment.","addition_date":"2015-08-03T09:35:44Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:16:05.786804Z","tool_type":["Web API"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:needle-api-ebi","credit":[{"name":"BioCatalogue","typeEntity":"Project","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"https://www.biocatalogue.org"},{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/support/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/services/psa/emboss_needle_rest"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["jdispatcher"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Pairwise sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491"}]}],"name":"needle-api (EBI)","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"jdispatcher","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkv1352","metadata":{"abstract":"New technologies are revolutionising biological research and its applications by making it easier and cheaper to generate ever-greater volumes and types of data. In response, the services and infrastructure of the European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI, www.ebi.ac.UK) are continually expanding: total disk capacity increases significantly every year to keep pace with demand (75 petabytes as of December 2015), and interoperability between resources remains a strategic priority. Since 2014 we have launched two new resources: the European Variation Archive for genetic variation data and EMPIAR for two-dimensional electron microscopy data, as well as a Resource Description Framework platform. We also launched the Embassy Cloud service, which allows users to run large analyses in a virtual environment next to EMBL-EBI's vast public d